{
  "core_message": "Mary Celeste’s abandoned voyage remains the most enduring maritime mystery.",
  "mood": "curious",
  "title": "10‑day mystery: Mary Celeste drifted crewless, cargo untouched",
  "description": "Mary Celeste was a Canadian‑built brigantine discovered drifting near the Azores in 1872 with all supplies intact and no crew aboard. Despite exhaustive investigations, the reason for its abandonment remains unsolved. This short explores the ship’s history, the eerie find, the theories that have emerged, and why the mystery endures.\n\nKey points:\n- Built in 1861, sailed under American flag.\n- Found drifting with lifeboat missing.\n- Logbook stopped ten days earlier.\n- No crew ever seen again.\n- Multiple theories: alcohol fumes, storms, giant squid, etc.\n\nBased on the Wikipedia article \"Mary Celeste\" (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mary_Celeste), licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.\n\nImages from Wikimedia Commons:\nGonave.jpg (NASA, Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gonave.jpg\nMary Celeste NYTimes 1873February26.png (Boston Post, Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mary_Celeste_NYTimes_1873February26.png\nLap desk of Captain Benjamin Briggs from the Mary Celeste (PEM M6557) 02.jpg (Crawdad Blues, CC0): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lap_desk_of_Captain_Benjamin_Briggs_from_the_Mary_Celeste_(PEM_M6557)_02.jpg\nArthur Conan Doyle by Herbert Rose Barraud 1893.jpg (Herbert Rose Barraud (1845 - c1896), Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arthur_Conan_Doyle_by_Herbert_Rose_Barraud_1893.jpg\nVillageview.jpg (Dan Conlin, CC BY-SA 3.0): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Villageview.jpg\nMary Celeste as Amazon in 1861 (cropped).jpg (Unconfirmed, possibly Honore Pellegrin (1800 – c.1870). This speculative attribu, Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mary_Celeste_as_Amazon_in_1861_(cropped).jpg\nSir James Cochrane 1841-1877.jpg (Unknown author Unknown author, Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_James_Cochrane_1841-1877.jpg\nGeorge McCord - New York Harbor.jpg (George McCord, Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:George_McCord_-_New_York_Harbor.jpg",
